WEBVTT

00:00:14.080 --> 00:00:15.500
You can do it!

00:00:19.250 --> 00:00:20.330
There!

00:00:21.330 --> 00:00:22.950
Go!

00:00:22.950 --> 00:00:24.500
Stop him!

00:00:24.500 --> 00:00:25.580
Okay!

00:00:35.660 --> 00:00:38.450
All right! Another point!

00:00:38.450 --> 00:00:40.540
That's his fifth one!

00:00:40.540 --> 00:00:42.580
Albert is really amazing.

00:00:42.580 --> 00:00:44.620
Don't you think he could go pro?

00:00:47.950 --> 00:00:49.620
Hmm?

00:02:34.370 --> 00:02:36.250
Huh?!

00:02:36.250 --> 00:02:37.910
Is that so?!

00:02:37.910 --> 00:02:39.620
Amazing!

00:02:39.620 --> 00:02:43.910
By the way, do you have a girlfriend Albert?!

00:02:43.910 --> 00:02:46.040
Oh! I want to know, too!

00:02:46.040 --> 00:02:47.410
I'm super curious!

00:02:47.410 --> 00:02:48.660
Tell us! Tell us!

00:02:48.660 --> 00:02:51.290
Well, which is it?!

00:02:51.290 --> 00:02:53.000
Want to see?

00:02:53.000 --> 00:02:58.120
Julia Bush. She's a world-famous
opera singer and model.

00:02:58.120 --> 00:02:59.370
That's...

00:02:59.370 --> 00:03:05.080
That's right. She's the mother of our
star transfer student, Albert Bush.

00:03:05.080 --> 00:03:08.040
Wow. She's amazing.

00:03:08.040 --> 00:03:09.910
Not that interested?

00:03:09.910 --> 00:03:12.700
Huh? No, I just don't really get it...

00:03:12.700 --> 00:03:17.660
Hmm? You're always pretty cool, Annie.

00:03:17.660 --> 00:03:21.370
A formidable rival has
appeared. Right, Roddy?

00:03:27.120 --> 00:03:33.750
Lately, everyone has only been
talking about the new kid, Albert.

00:03:33.750 --> 00:03:35.660
How annoying.

00:04:04.830 --> 00:04:06.450
Albert?!

00:04:06.450 --> 00:04:09.000
Call me Al. Everyone does.

00:04:09.000 --> 00:04:10.950
Why are you here?

00:04:10.950 --> 00:04:15.660
I was looking around the school
and I heard a pretty voice.

00:04:15.660 --> 00:04:17.700
P-Pretty?

00:04:17.700 --> 00:04:19.700
It was beautiful.

00:04:23.330 --> 00:04:26.450
Isn't singing nice?

00:04:26.450 --> 00:04:28.910
It seems so human.

00:04:28.910 --> 00:04:32.120
Really? Even birds sing.

00:04:32.120 --> 00:04:36.870
I see. Then maybe birds
want to become humans, too?

00:04:36.870 --> 00:04:41.580
Come to think of it, my mother once
said she wanted to become a bird.

00:04:41.580 --> 00:04:42.620
Huh?

00:04:42.620 --> 00:04:46.750
She wanted to become a bird,
spending her entire life singing every day.

00:04:46.750 --> 00:04:49.080
That's right!

00:04:49.080 --> 00:04:50.540
What is it all of a sudden?

00:04:50.540 --> 00:04:52.830
We're doing a home party next week.

00:04:52.830 --> 00:04:54.540
You should come!

00:04:54.540 --> 00:04:55.950
Home party?

00:04:55.950 --> 00:04:57.580
Yeah. Come.

00:04:57.580 --> 00:05:00.950
I want to introduce my mother
to you--how about it?

00:05:03.500 --> 00:05:05.250
I'll think about it.

00:05:08.500 --> 00:05:09.910
Good work, everyone!

00:05:09.910 --> 00:05:11.750
Good work!

00:05:11.750 --> 00:05:13.200
See you next week.

00:05:27.830 --> 00:05:28.910
What?

00:05:31.910 --> 00:05:33.450
Noo!

00:05:54.040 --> 00:05:55.450
This is really nice!

00:05:55.450 --> 00:05:56.540
Gonna buy it?!

00:05:56.540 --> 00:05:59.040
This one is nice, too.

00:05:59.040 --> 00:06:00.750
U-Um...

00:06:00.750 --> 00:06:01.910
What?

00:06:01.910 --> 00:06:06.200
What kind of clothes would
be nice for a formal event?

00:06:06.200 --> 00:06:09.160
Oh, for the up-and-coming party!

00:06:09.160 --> 00:06:13.000
I feel like you'd probably already
have a lot of nice clothes.

00:06:14.450 --> 00:06:18.330
I don't really go to parties much...

00:06:18.330 --> 00:06:21.700
No problem. Let's look together!

00:06:21.700 --> 00:06:23.080
Thanks.

00:06:23.080 --> 00:06:25.120
Wow! Sounds fun!

00:06:25.120 --> 00:06:27.580
I love choosing outfits for other people!

00:06:27.580 --> 00:06:31.540
No way. Are you planning on
forcing your weird tastes on her?

00:06:31.540 --> 00:06:32.700
What do you mean weird?!

00:06:32.700 --> 00:06:35.120
I'd rather you say my style has character!

00:06:35.120 --> 00:06:37.250
Oh, my. My apologies.

00:06:37.250 --> 00:06:39.000
Oh, look at that.

00:06:50.500 --> 00:06:53.450
Is that Albert's mother?

00:06:53.450 --> 00:06:54.870
She looks so young.

00:06:54.870 --> 00:06:56.950
Isn't she almost 50 years old now?

00:06:56.950 --> 00:06:58.750
She's a witch! A witch!

00:07:01.700 --> 00:07:04.580
She has a big chest...

00:07:07.330 --> 00:07:09.120
That's what bothers you?!

00:07:23.620 --> 00:07:25.540
Really, how wonderful!

00:07:25.540 --> 00:07:29.330
Your adult appeal is even
more polished than before!

00:07:29.330 --> 00:07:31.160
What a way with words.

00:07:31.160 --> 00:07:33.750
However, I am Julia Bush.

00:07:33.750 --> 00:07:36.120
This level is still not satisfactory.

00:07:36.120 --> 00:07:38.750
Please work with me next week, as well.

00:07:38.750 --> 00:07:40.620
Y-Yeah.

00:07:40.620 --> 00:07:43.410
Then, please take care.
I will be taking my leave.

00:07:45.700 --> 00:07:48.950
Do you think something
will change in just one week?

00:07:48.950 --> 00:07:54.750
Who knows? Well, I'm sure she's
aware of the state of her own throat.

00:08:08.830 --> 00:08:11.290
L-Like this?

00:08:13.120 --> 00:08:14.290
What is it?

00:08:14.290 --> 00:08:16.910
Is there something wrong with your body?

00:08:16.910 --> 00:08:19.540
Th-That's not it...

00:08:19.540 --> 00:08:22.410
Our bodies are different from a human's.

00:08:22.410 --> 00:08:26.790
We don't even know the limits
of our own bodies ourselves.

00:08:26.790 --> 00:08:29.580
Report any irregularities immediately.

00:08:32.450 --> 00:08:33.750
Hmm?

00:08:33.750 --> 00:08:36.450
Hey, you. Don't look through
things without permission!

00:08:36.450 --> 00:08:40.120
You're suddenly into brand name things.

00:08:40.120 --> 00:08:44.410
Nice, like a human of the nouveau rich.

00:08:44.410 --> 00:08:45.790
Hmph!

00:08:48.500 --> 00:08:50.660
This is the third case.

00:08:50.660 --> 00:08:53.870
The victims are all women
in their teens and 20s.

00:08:53.870 --> 00:08:56.700
They all died from having
their throats ripped out.

00:08:56.700 --> 00:09:00.950
A case where the dead truly can't talk.

00:09:00.950 --> 00:09:03.120
Don't make jokes that aren't funny.

00:09:03.120 --> 00:09:05.950
So strict. So scary.

00:09:05.950 --> 00:09:10.370
The camera was broken and it was
unable to record the culprit, right?

00:09:10.370 --> 00:09:12.370
What were the jobs of the victims?!

00:09:13.620 --> 00:09:15.620
The first one was a musical actress.

00:09:15.620 --> 00:09:18.040
Second one a television announcer.

00:09:18.040 --> 00:09:22.250
Third one was the vocalist of a rock band.

00:09:22.250 --> 00:09:25.410
The one thing in common...

00:09:25.410 --> 00:09:26.700
Their voices?!

00:09:37.500 --> 00:09:39.750
Still not good enough?

00:09:39.750 --> 00:09:40.700
Yes.

00:09:40.700 --> 00:09:43.410
The vocal chord samples you brought.

00:09:43.410 --> 00:09:46.330
They are all unusable.

00:09:46.330 --> 00:09:49.080
What's the problem?!

00:09:49.080 --> 00:09:51.620
I don't know how to explain...

00:09:51.620 --> 00:09:55.910
Fine. That just means I need
to bring more samples, right?

00:09:55.910 --> 00:10:01.750
Please find something lively
that will catch my interest.

00:10:03.870 --> 00:10:09.080
Goodness. I no longer
have any interest in you.

00:10:09.080 --> 00:10:11.370
In comparison...

00:10:12.750 --> 00:10:16.700
My next work might become a masterpiece!

00:10:23.290 --> 00:10:25.450
Woohoo!

00:10:34.290 --> 00:10:35.830
Too bad.

00:10:35.830 --> 00:10:39.540
I would have brought a swim suit
if I knew there was a pool.

00:10:39.540 --> 00:10:41.660
By the way, have you noticed?

00:10:41.660 --> 00:10:42.870
What?

00:10:42.870 --> 00:10:45.040
Over there.

00:10:45.040 --> 00:10:46.910
Oh!

00:10:46.910 --> 00:10:50.200
It seems he came along
since you decided to go, Annie.

00:10:50.200 --> 00:10:51.330
I see.

00:10:51.330 --> 00:10:53.620
Well? Enjoying the party?

00:10:53.620 --> 00:10:56.000
Yeah. Pretty well.

00:10:56.000 --> 00:10:57.330
You, Annie?

00:10:57.330 --> 00:10:59.830
Huh?! Oh. Yeah...

00:10:59.830 --> 00:11:02.410
I-I'm enjoying it.

00:11:02.410 --> 00:11:05.080
Hey, Albert. Where's your mother?

00:11:05.080 --> 00:11:08.870
Oh, she should be home soon.

00:11:08.870 --> 00:11:10.830
Speak of the devil...

00:11:16.160 --> 00:11:17.370
Mother!

00:11:19.700 --> 00:11:22.660
Mother, there is someone
I'd like to introduce to you.

00:11:22.660 --> 00:11:24.500
My classmate, Annabella.

00:11:24.500 --> 00:11:26.750
I told you about her before.

00:11:26.750 --> 00:11:28.330
Nice to meet you.

00:11:32.580 --> 00:11:36.410
You have a wonderful body.

00:11:36.410 --> 00:11:39.080
I'm so jealous of youth.

00:11:39.080 --> 00:11:40.580
That's right, Mother!

00:11:40.580 --> 00:11:43.700
She has the best voice!
You should listen!

00:11:43.700 --> 00:11:45.160
Huh? Wait a second!

00:11:45.160 --> 00:11:47.040
Even if you say that suddenly...

00:11:47.040 --> 00:11:48.700
It's fine. It's fine!

00:12:16.200 --> 00:12:19.160
What a wonderful voice, Annabella!

00:12:19.160 --> 00:12:23.500
You have potential. I can tell.

00:12:23.500 --> 00:12:26.750
That's right! You should come audition.

00:12:26.750 --> 00:12:28.450
Audition?

00:12:28.450 --> 00:12:32.870
A producer I know is looking
for new upcoming talent.

00:12:32.870 --> 00:12:35.450
Even if you say that suddenly...

00:12:35.450 --> 00:12:37.160
You should try it out.

00:12:37.160 --> 00:12:41.040
You'd definitely pass! I'm sure of it!

00:12:43.080 --> 00:12:44.540
Thank you.

00:12:58.830 --> 00:13:00.500
Hmm.

00:13:06.040 --> 00:13:09.410
What is it? An abnormality in your body?

00:13:09.410 --> 00:13:11.040
Y-Yeah.

00:13:11.040 --> 00:13:15.580
Actually, lately, my heart
will race sometimes.

00:13:15.580 --> 00:13:17.700
Your heart races?!

00:13:17.700 --> 00:13:20.910
And my cheeks get warm.

00:13:20.910 --> 00:13:23.500
Is there something wrong with my body?

00:13:28.910 --> 00:13:32.660
Goodness. Why are you saying
things like a normal human?

00:13:32.660 --> 00:13:34.410
Shut up!

00:13:34.410 --> 00:13:36.700
I'm dying!

00:13:36.700 --> 00:13:38.410
"My heart races!"

00:13:38.410 --> 00:13:40.000
Shut up!

00:13:43.120 --> 00:13:44.950
An undamaged surveillance camera?

00:13:44.950 --> 00:13:46.410
I can't believe you found one.

00:13:46.410 --> 00:13:50.620
Yes. And we've discovered
the culprit's method of attack.

00:13:50.620 --> 00:13:53.500
Do you know what a blue note attack is?

00:13:54.870 --> 00:13:56.580
Blue, what?

00:13:56.580 --> 00:14:03.330
It's a sound wave that can destroy
hard disks by vibrating its components.

00:14:03.330 --> 00:14:10.040
However, to do so, you need a powerful
oscillator. In other words, a speaker.

00:14:10.040 --> 00:14:11.870
Oh, here it is.

00:14:16.830 --> 00:14:19.290
As expected, the use of sound.

00:14:25.120 --> 00:14:26.000
What is that?

00:14:26.000 --> 00:14:27.200
Zooming in.

00:14:34.700 --> 00:14:37.540
Welcome, Annabella.

00:14:37.540 --> 00:14:39.410
Thank you for coming.

00:14:39.410 --> 00:14:41.790
Sorry for suddenly asking,
but please follow me.

00:14:41.790 --> 00:14:43.540
Oh. Yes!

00:14:43.540 --> 00:14:46.500
Al, wait outside.

00:14:46.500 --> 00:14:50.000
I have some advice for her,
between us women.

00:14:50.000 --> 00:14:53.910
I see. Annie, I'll see you later.

00:14:53.910 --> 00:14:55.500
I'm rooting for you!

00:14:55.500 --> 00:14:57.950
Thank you, Albert.

00:15:03.290 --> 00:15:05.750
There's no one here?

00:15:05.750 --> 00:15:10.870
Yes. This is a soundproof room
so they won't hear us outside.

00:15:10.870 --> 00:15:11.700
Huh?

00:15:11.700 --> 00:15:14.500
That's why it's a perfect place...

00:15:14.500 --> 00:15:17.750
...to take your throat.

00:15:24.370 --> 00:15:25.660
Wha--?!

00:15:29.120 --> 00:15:31.120
Th-This is--?!

00:15:35.910 --> 00:15:38.080
Oh? You're a tough one.

00:15:38.080 --> 00:15:41.500
That's fine. It's proof
of your youthfulness and health.

00:15:42.750 --> 00:15:44.540
Oh, Julia.

00:15:44.540 --> 00:15:46.500
I thought the stage test was next week.

00:15:46.500 --> 00:15:49.200
Shut up! You're in the way!

00:15:49.200 --> 00:15:51.080
M-Monster!

00:15:56.910 --> 00:15:58.950
I won't let you escape.

00:16:06.790 --> 00:16:08.700
Mother! Annie!

00:16:21.250 --> 00:16:24.040
Mother! Annie!

00:16:24.040 --> 00:16:25.200
Al!

00:16:25.200 --> 00:16:27.120
Thank goodness you're safe, Mother.

00:16:27.120 --> 00:16:28.200
Where is Annie?!

00:16:28.200 --> 00:16:29.250
That girl is...

00:16:29.250 --> 00:16:30.790
Run! Al!

00:16:30.790 --> 00:16:32.120
Huh?!

00:16:36.790 --> 00:16:40.120
Goodnight, my sweet Al.

00:16:40.120 --> 00:16:43.370
Sleep until everything is over.

00:16:46.410 --> 00:16:51.540
Where are you, Annabella?

00:16:51.540 --> 00:16:56.250
Now. Come on out, my sweet kitten.

00:17:00.120 --> 00:17:02.450
Damn you, you bitch of a cat!

00:17:04.450 --> 00:17:05.540
I got it!

00:17:05.540 --> 00:17:07.910
The concert hall in East 32!

00:17:07.910 --> 00:17:10.870
To think that such a famous
singer was our culprit.

00:17:11.950 --> 00:17:13.500
Zooming in.

00:17:15.040 --> 00:17:17.330
It's Julia Bush!

00:17:17.330 --> 00:17:20.700
A fire has broken out at the concert hall.

00:17:20.700 --> 00:17:22.870
Currently, the fire trucks are on the way.

00:17:22.870 --> 00:17:23.730
Fire?!

00:17:23.730 --> 00:17:24.700
Oh, my?

00:17:24.700 --> 00:17:27.290
That sounds awfully fishy.

00:17:27.290 --> 00:17:29.200
Just hurry up!

00:17:33.250 --> 00:17:35.160
There's no point in hiding!

00:17:35.160 --> 00:17:37.160
I've locked all the doors!

00:17:37.160 --> 00:17:39.080
There's nowhere to run!

00:17:42.000 --> 00:17:43.250
I see.

00:17:43.250 --> 00:17:44.910
Well, it can't be helped.

00:17:44.910 --> 00:17:48.000
Though, I didn't want to involve my son.

00:18:00.500 --> 00:18:02.120
Stop it!

00:18:03.120 --> 00:18:04.410
You're--?!

00:18:04.410 --> 00:18:06.330
Is that Annabella's voice?!

00:18:06.330 --> 00:18:08.410
Why do you look like that?!

00:18:08.410 --> 00:18:11.620
I think you look pretty strange yourself!

00:18:12.950 --> 00:18:17.370
Even so, you fell for my trap pretty easily.

00:18:17.370 --> 00:18:21.200
Did you really think I'd kill my own son?

00:18:21.200 --> 00:18:24.870
Seems the little girl is still just that.

00:18:24.870 --> 00:18:28.290
Oh, that dress looks so good on you.

00:18:28.290 --> 00:18:29.950
It's perfect.

00:18:29.950 --> 00:18:32.330
Don't joke around!

00:18:32.330 --> 00:18:37.080
Don't think a little girl like you
can beat me, Julia Bush!

00:18:42.000 --> 00:18:43.370
This is--?!

00:18:43.370 --> 00:18:47.500
Don't you know?! I'm using
the stage's reverberation.

00:18:47.500 --> 00:18:49.830
See? Here, too!

00:18:57.500 --> 00:19:00.290
Now! What will you do, little girl?!

00:19:00.290 --> 00:19:04.870
Even in that form, she is still
Al's mother. What should I do?

00:19:07.290 --> 00:19:10.910
Hurry up and die!

00:19:10.910 --> 00:19:12.040
Shit!

00:19:14.790 --> 00:19:16.950
Where are you aiming?!

00:19:18.200 --> 00:19:19.870
I'm aiming for you!

00:19:26.790 --> 00:19:31.450
How dare you... To my beautiful face!

00:19:33.120 --> 00:19:39.000
Now! The moving finale!

00:20:08.660 --> 00:20:11.080
Sorry, lady.

00:20:11.080 --> 00:20:14.370
Our bodies don't die.

00:20:16.790 --> 00:20:19.410
Mother...?

00:20:19.410 --> 00:20:20.790
Al?!

00:20:33.000 --> 00:20:35.580
M-Monster!

00:21:08.160 --> 00:21:10.040
Beautiful...

00:21:13.790 --> 00:21:15.410
W-Wait!

00:21:17.450 --> 00:21:19.200
Hey!

00:21:19.200 --> 00:21:21.200
Anyone there?!

00:21:30.660 --> 00:21:34.500
Amazing. Such perfect beauty!

00:21:40.580 --> 00:21:42.290
That's some taste you have.

00:21:42.290 --> 00:21:43.700
Huh?

00:21:49.450 --> 00:21:53.120
Hey, hey. Did you hear? Al transferred.

00:21:53.120 --> 00:21:54.370
I see.

00:21:54.370 --> 00:21:56.370
That's too bad.
